      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.49,
          "end": 4.53,
          "en": "Instructor: To build our own observable, I'll go",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 4.53,
          "end": 8.04,
          "en": "into that home component and there in ngOnInit",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 8.04,
          "end": 10.77,
          "en": "I wanna build a new observable.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 10.77,
          "end": 14.67,
          "en": "Now observables are a feature that's not baked",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 14.67,
          "end": 16.95,
          "en": "into JavaScript or type script.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 16.95,
          "end": 20.64,
          "en": "Instead they're added by a package named rxjs",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 20.64,
          "end": 22.86,
          "en": "And that's why in Angular projects",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 22.86,
          "end": 24.78,
          "en": "if you have a look at package.json",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 24.78,
          "end": 29.283,
          "en": "which lists all your dependencies, you find rxjs here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 31.26,
          "end": 33.63,
          "en": "Now in the home component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 33.63,
          "end": 36.6,
          "en": "I want to build my own observable here in ngOnInit",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 36.6,
          "end": 39.06,
          "en": "And for that we can import something",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 39.06,
          "end": 41.22,
          "en": "from that rxjs package.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 41.22,
          "end": 43.95,
          "en": "So let's import from rxjs",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 43.95,
          "end": 46.44,
          "en": "and we don't need to do that when using observables",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 46.44,
          "end": 48.21,
          "en": "because thanks to type script",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 48.21,
          "end": 50.61,
          "en": "it understands that parents is an observable",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 50.61,
          "end": 52.56,
          "en": "and they offer it knows we can subscribe there",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 52.56,
          "end": 55.92,
          "en": "and we never need to explicitly inform it about the type.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 55.92,
          "end": 57.9,
          "en": "But if we want to create a new observable",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 57.9,
          "end": 61.14,
          "en": "we need certain features from that rxjs package",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 61.14,
          "end": 64.56,
          "en": "To be precise that rxjs package gives us different ways",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 64.56,
          "end": 66.36,
          "en": "of creating a new observable.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 66.36,
          "end": 71.36,
          "en": "And one of the easiest ways is the, interval method.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 71.49,
          "end": 74.43,
          "en": "The interval function, you can just import interval",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 74.43,
          "end": 78.78,
          "en": "like this and then here you can call interval",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 78.78,
          "end": 81.33,
          "en": "and pass in a number that is a bit",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 81.33,
          "end": 84.21000000000001,
          "en": "like set interval where you pass a number in",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 84.21000000000001,
          "end": 89.21000000000001,
          "en": "milliseconds that will fire an event every X milliseconds.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 89.73,
          "end": 91.65,
          "en": "So if I pass 1000 here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 91.65,
          "end": 95.7,
          "en": "then every second a new event will be emitted.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 95.7,
          "end": 97.22999999999999,
          "en": "Now this gives us an observable",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 97.22999999999999,
          "end": 100.25999999999999,
          "en": "and therefore we can subscribe to the observable here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 100.25999999999999,
          "end": 104.61,
          "en": "And there, I can now get my count.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 104.61,
          "end": 106.17,
          "en": "You can name this whatever you want",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 106.17,
          "end": 109.08,
          "en": "and handle this or use this inside of this function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 109.08,
          "end": 112.41,
          "en": "So I'm passing an anonymous function here to subscribe.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 112.41,
          "end": 115.35,
          "en": "That's the first argument we can pass to subscribe.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 115.35,
          "end": 119.67,
          "en": "It's the handler for all the data values that are emitted.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 119.67,
          "end": 123.33,
          "en": "So I passed this in it gets the value that is emitted",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 123.33,
          "end": 126.09,
          "en": "as an argument and I just named his argument count",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 126.09,
          "end": 128.58,
          "en": "because it turns out it will be an incrementing number",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 128.58,
          "end": 132.63,
          "en": "for interval. We'll later also build an observable entirely",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 132.63,
          "end": 135.39,
          "en": "from scratch where we fully control the emitted values.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 135.39,
          "end": 138.75,
          "en": "Here we'll take this half measure, which is a built",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 138.75,
          "end": 142.35,
          "en": "in function that gives us an observable, but still it's more",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 142.35,
          "end": 145.5,
          "en": "from the ground up than the ones angular ships with.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 145.5,
          "end": 146.52,
          "en": "So here we have interval",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 146.52,
          "end": 149.01,
          "en": "which will fire a new value every second.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 149.01,
          "end": 153.42000000000002,
          "en": "And in this function here, I will simply console log count.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 153.42000000000002,
          "end": 155.43,
          "en": "So the idea now is that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 155.43,
          "end": 157.41,
          "en": "we get a new value emitted every",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 157.41,
          "end": 160.14,
          "en": "second and we lock that to the console.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 160.14,
          "end": 161.97,
          "en": "Now let's save all files",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 161.97,
          "end": 165.663,
          "en": "and open the developer tools here in our browser.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 167.22,
          "end": 168.053,
          "en": "And there let's go",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 168.053,
          "end": 171.03,
          "en": "to the JavaScript console and navigate to the homepage.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 171.03,
          "end": 174.12,
          "en": "And there you should now see incrementing values",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 174.12,
          "end": 177.27,
          "en": "being locked to the console, one value every second.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 177.27,
          "end": 178.5,
          "en": "And that of course comes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 178.5,
          "end": 182.64,
          "en": "from that interval function that gives us an observable.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 182.64,
          "end": 185.91,
          "en": "And again, this is not an observable we built entirely",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 185.91,
          "end": 188.253,
          "en": "from the ground up, but it's pretty close.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 189.66,
          "end": 193.11,
          "en": "Now when I navigate away now to user one",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 193.11,
          "end": 195.66,
          "en": "you see that this keeps on counting",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 195.66,
          "end": 198.18,
          "en": "and that is something you have to be aware of.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 198.18,
          "end": 202.74,
          "en": "Observables don't necessarily stop emitting values just",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 202.74,
          "end": 205.35,
          "en": "because you're not interested in them anymore.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 205.35,
          "end": 208.41,
          "en": "There are certain observables that emit a value once",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 208.41,
          "end": 209.37,
          "en": "and they're done.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 209.37,
          "end": 210.57,
          "en": "Like for example",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 210.57,
          "end": 213,
          "en": "an HTTP request where you get back a response",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 213,
          "end": 216.54,
          "en": "something you'll see later in the HTP module of this course.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 216.54,
          "end": 220.07999999999998,
          "en": "But there are other observables that keep on emitting values",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 220.07999999999998,
          "end": 223.53,
          "en": "and to stop that and their effort to prevent memory leaks",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 223.53,
          "end": 226.11,
          "en": "which you would otherwise introduce If that keeps on",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 226.11,
          "end": 229.11,
          "en": "emitting whilst you're not interested in it anymore",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 229.11,
          "end": 231.63,
          "en": "you should unsubscribe from any observable",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 231.63,
          "end": 234.72,
          "en": "in which values you are no longer interested.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 234.72,
          "end": 237.36,
          "en": "And that's really important because before we do that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 237.36,
          "end": 240.21,
          "en": "watch what happens if I go back to the homepage",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 240.21,
          "end": 242.67,
          "en": "I'm on user one, I wasn't home before.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 242.67,
          "end": 244.77,
          "en": "Now I go back to home.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 244.77,
          "end": 247.35,
          "en": "What you now see is a new observable started.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 247.35,
          "end": 250.08,
          "en": "So we have the old one going on and a new one.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 250.08,
          "end": 252.09,
          "en": "And of course we can repeat that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 252.09,
          "end": 254.82,
          "en": "We get more and more observables counting.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 254.82,
          "end": 257.1,
          "en": "And that of course is very bad.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 257.1,
          "end": 260.251,
          "en": "If that happens behind the scenes. You quickly run out",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 260.251,
          "end": 262.92,
          "en": "of resources and you slow down your app.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 262.92,
          "end": 265.05,
          "en": "You introduce a memory leak here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 265.05,
          "end": 267.78,
          "en": "because your memory gets occupied a lot",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 267.78,
          "end": 269.52,
          "en": "by data you don't need.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 269.52,
          "end": 271.71,
          "en": "So you definitely need to clear that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 271.71,
          "end": 275.49,
          "en": "And to do that, we should store our subscriptions.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 275.49,
          "end": 280.44,
          "en": "And here I'll then name this first Obs subscription.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 280.44,
          "end": 281.64,
          "en": "You can name it whatever you want.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 281.64,
          "end": 284.4,
          "en": "And the type of this private property",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 284.4,
          "end": 288.27,
          "en": "of the home component will be subscription",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 288.27,
          "end": 291.75,
          "en": "and subscription also needs to be imported from rxjs.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 291.75,
          "end": 293.97,
          "en": "So make sure to add the import.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 293.97,
          "end": 294.96,
          "en": "And now here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 294.96,
          "end": 298.56,
          "en": "subscribe actually returns such as subscription.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 298.56,
          "end": 303.56,
          "en": "So when we subscribe, we can store that subscription",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 303.84,
          "end": 307.38,
          "en": "in our first ops subscription property.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 307.38,
          "end": 309.24,
          "en": "So we're not storing the observable here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 309.24,
          "end": 312.3,
          "en": "that's the observable, but we instantly subscribe here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 312.3,
          "end": 314.85,
          "en": "and therefore we store whatever subscriber turns",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 314.85,
          "end": 317.76,
          "en": "and subscribe returns a subscription.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 317.76,
          "end": 320.67,
          "en": "Now the idea behind storing the subscription simply is",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 320.67,
          "end": 323.7,
          "en": "that we now can also implement on Destroy here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 323.7,
          "end": 326.67,
          "en": "which you need to import from @ angular core.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 326.67,
          "end": 331.26,
          "en": "And that forces us to add the ngOnDestroy Lifecycle Hook.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 331.26,
          "end": 333.33,
          "en": "And inside of ngOnDestroy",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 333.33,
          "end": 337.83,
          "en": "we can now use our subscription and call unsubscribe.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 337.83,
          "end": 340.47,
          "en": "And that means that whenever we leave that component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 340.47,
          "end": 342.21,
          "en": "we clear that subscription",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 342.21,
          "end": 345.27,
          "en": "and therefore we prevent memory leaks",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 345.27,
          "end": 348.39,
          "en": "because we're not keeping old subscriptions around.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 348.39,
          "end": 349.65,
          "en": "Now if you save that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 349.65,
          "end": 354.65,
          "en": "and reload the app you see our observable starts again.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 355.26,
          "end": 358.68,
          "en": "But if I navigate away, we get no new values.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 358.68,
          "end": 360.9,
          "en": "If I go back, it starts at zero again",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 360.9,
          "end": 364.35,
          "en": "but the old observable is dead because we unsubscribe.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 364.35,
          "end": 366.39,
          "en": "And that's an important step.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 366.39,
          "end": 369.84,
          "en": "So this is an important step towards",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 369.84,
          "end": 373.652,
          "en": "understanding observables. One common question I get is",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 373.652,
          "end": 376.2,
          "en": "okay, we unsubscribe here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 376.2,
          "end": 378.72,
          "en": "Why don't we unsubscribe in the user component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 130,
          "start": 378.72,
          "end": 381.09,
          "en": "here where we also set up a subscription.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 131,
          "start": 381.09,
          "end": 383.1,
          "en": "And that is a valid question.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 132,
          "start": 383.1,
          "end": 385.77,
          "en": "The answer simply is Angular does that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 133,
          "start": 385.77,
          "end": 389.73,
          "en": "for you for the observables provided by Angular",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 134,
          "start": 389.73,
          "end": 393.36,
          "en": "like parents but also any other observable you'll",
          "zh": ""
